DAY 50 - PART A: THEORY
Helm: Charts, Values, Releases
Time: 40 minutes
==================================================================

Week 8 runs on your local kind cluster with the ingress controller
(kind-ingress.yaml from Day 19). Cloud is optional on Day 56.


1. THE PROBLEM HELM SOLVES
--------------------------
A real app = 10-30 YAML files (Deployment, Service, Ingress, ConfigMap,
Secret, HPA, PDB, ServiceAccount, RBAC ...), slightly different per
environment. Copying files per environment (Day 13) doesn't scale.
Installing third-party software (Prometheus, cert-manager) from raw
YAML is painful to upgrade.


2. HELM CONCEPTS
----------------
  Chart       a package: templates + default values + metadata
  Values      settings you pass in (values.yaml, --set, -f file)
  Release     one installed instance of a chart in a namespace, with
              a name (you can install the same chart many times)
  Revision    each install/upgrade/rollback creates a numbered
              revision (stored as a Secret in the namespace)
  Repository  where charts are published (HTTP index or OCI registry)

  templates + values  --render-->  plain Kubernetes YAML  --apply-->


3. CHART LAYOUT
---------------
  mychart/
    Chart.yaml          name, version (chart), appVersion (app)
    values.yaml         defaults
    templates/          Go templates -> YAML
      deployment.yaml
      service.yaml
      _helpers.tpl      reusable snippets (names, labels)
      NOTES.txt         printed after install
    charts/             dependencies (subcharts)


4. KEY COMMANDS
---------------
  helm repo add NAME URL ; helm repo update
  helm search repo KEYWORD
  helm show values CHART > values.yaml
  helm install RELEASE CHART -n NS --create-namespace -f my-values.yaml
  helm upgrade --install RELEASE CHART -f my-values.yaml   (idempotent)
  helm list -A
  helm get values|manifest RELEASE
  helm history RELEASE
  helm rollback RELEASE REVISION
  helm uninstall RELEASE
  helm template RELEASE CHART -f values.yaml   (render only, no install)
  helm diff upgrade ...   (plugin: show changes before upgrading)

OCI charts: helm install x oci://registry/path/chart --version 1.2.3


5. VALUES PRECEDENCE (last wins)
--------------------------------
  chart values.yaml  <  -f file1.yaml  <  -f file2.yaml  <  --set k=v
Pattern: values-dev.yaml, values-prod.yaml per environment.


KEY POINTS TO REMEMBER
----------------------
- Chart = package, values = settings, release = installed instance.
- upgrade --install + values files per environment.
- helm template shows exactly what will be applied.
